ing image analysis**\\n\\nI need to ensure any answer I provide is safe and cautious. I can visually see a large abnormality, but I should avoid jumping to conclusions based on that without proper tools for analysis. The image appears to show a significant right renal mass, but I need to be careful and focus on confirming details from the attached image and using the prototype pipeline for a clearer understanding.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]]### Clinical picture\n- I ran the **specialized kidney cancer detection prototype** on the CT image you attached.\n- The pipeline output was:\n  - **Kidney cancer class:** kidney_tumor\n  - **Confidence:** 99.998%\n- Independent of the prototype, the image itself also appears to show a **large abnormal-looking mass in the right kidney region** on this slice, which is **concerning** and fits with your prior record.\n\n### Most likely possibilities\n1. **Right kidney tumor / renal mass is present on this scan**\n   - Both the **image appearance** and the **prototype pipeline** point in that direction.\n2. **This could be related to your known RCC history**\n   - Given your prior right-sided kidney cancer follow-up, pink urine, fatigue, weight loss, and worsening right-sided pain, this is a serious concern.\n3. **Other kidney abnormalities are less likely than a mass here**\n   - Symptoms like blood in the urine can also happen with stones or infection, but this image is not reassuring.\n\n### Confidence / uncertainty note\n- I am **highly concerned by this scan**.\n- That said, this is still **not a formal radiology diagnosis**. A proper interpretation needs your treating clinicians and official imaging review.\n- The prototype result is strong, but it should be treated as **supporting evidence**, not final proof.\n\n### Red flags / urgent concerns\nBecause you now have:\n- **pink urine**\n- **worsening right-sided back/flank pain**\n- **fatigue**\n- **possible weight loss**\n- and a **concerning CT image**\n\nI think you should **contact your urologist/oncology team immediately today**.  \nIf you cannot reach them promptly, or if the bleeding/pain is worsening, go to **urgent care or the ER today**.\n\nGo to the ER sooner if you have:\n- worsening blood in urine or clots\n- severe pain\n- fever/chills\n- vomiting\n- weakness, dizziness, fainting\n- trouble urinating\n\n### Recommended next questions\n1. Do you already have a **radiology report** for this CT?\n2. When exactly was this CT done?\n3. Is the urine still pink/red today?\n4. Are you having **clots, fever, or trouble passing urine**?\n5. Do you want help sending an **urgent message** to your doctor right now?\n\n### Suggested tool/skill use\n- The kidney imaging prototype has already been used and it is **concerning**.\n- The next important step is **real-world urgent clinical follow-up**, not more screening.\n\n## Bottom line\nYes — **I would be worried enough to act on this now**. This scan is **not reassuring**, and in the context of your symptoms and history, you should seek **same-day specialist or urgent evaluation**.\n\nIf you want, I can draft a **very short urgent message** you can send immediately, for example:\n\n> “I have a history of right kidney RCC follow-up. Over the last months I’ve had worsening right-sided flank/lower back pain, increasing fatigue, some weight loss, and last week I noticed pink urine. I’m concerned about progression/recurrence and need urgent review of my CT and labs. Can someone assess this today?”\n\nIf you want, I can make that message even shorter and ready to copy-paste.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_05b41355eb12ff050169b93dd6a2188191b621673728aa643d\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":20810,"output":758,"cacheRead":3584,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":25152,"cost":{"input":0.052025,"output":0.01137,"cacheRead":0.000896,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.064291}},"stopReason":"stop","t